  "title": "EU Kids Act and France's Social Media Ban",
  "summary": "The EU's new Kids Act bans social media access for children under 13, making it the first EU country to implement such a ban. France's Top Court struck down a social media ban for children under 15, setting a precedent for future policies. France has passed a law banning social media access for under-15s, and a New Mexico judge ordered the parent company to pay another $567m for the way it has harmed children.",
